3.3.1 Functional Requirements
1.	The system shall allow users to register and log in securely.
2.	The system shall maintain authenticated user sessions.
3.	The system shall allow users to create new resumes.
4.	The system shall allow users to save, edit, and delete resumes.
5.	The system shall allow users to select a resume context type.
6.	The system shall collect user information including personal details, education, work experience, skills, and achievements.
7.	The system shall process user inputs through a contextual processing engine.
8.	The system shall interface with a Large Language Model through an API for resume generation.
9.	The system shall generate context-appropriate resume content.
10.	The system shall display generated resumes in a formatted preview.
11.	The system shall allow users to export resumes in PDF format.
12.	The system shall store generated resumes for later access.
13.	The system shall allow administrators to view all registered users.
14.	The system shall allow administrators to manage user accounts.
15.	The system shall store all data in a relational database.
16.	The system shall validate all user input.
17.	The system shall restrict access to authorized users only.

3.3.2 Non-Functional Requirements
1.	The system shall process authentication requests within three seconds for most login attempts.
2.	The system shall generate resume content within five seconds for most requests.
3.	The system shall securely hash user passwords before storage.
4.	The system shall automatically log out inactive users after fifteen minutes.
5.	The system shall encrypt data transmitted between client and server.
6.	The system shall provide a responsive interface for desktop and mobile devices.
7.	The system shall support concurrent users without performance degradation.
8.	The system shall efficiently store and retrieve large volumes of resume data.
9.	The system shall allow API integration without service interruption.
10.	The system shall be modular to allow easy addition of new context types.
